Release v0.0.4 - i18n Support, .gitignore and Documentation Migration

This release introduces full internationalisation (i18n) to Auto4Git,
with automatic locale detection and built-in support for pt_BR (default)
and en_US (fallback). All user-facing messages are now routed through the
i18n layer — no string is left outside it. A .gitignore file is added and
all documentation is migrated to English as the canonical language.

Changes in this release:

i18n
- Automatic locale detection via $LANG / $LC_ALL / $LC_MESSAGES
- New detect_locale() function normalises system locale to pt_BR or en_US
- New t(key) translation helper with pt_BR → en_US fallback chain
- New i18n_get(locale, key) key-value store embedded at the end of the script
- All messages categorised by domain: prefix.*, usage.*, ssh.*, git.*,
  interactive.*, input.*, tag.*, legacy.*, proc.*, section.*, summary.*
- SSH tutorial fully i18n-ised in both pt_BR and en_US

.gitignore
- Added .gitignore covering: .msgtag / .msgcommit, editor and IDE folders,
  temporary files, OS-specific files, log and test artefacts

Documentation
- README migrated to English with i18n section and updated version badge
- CHANGELOG consolidated, translated to English and reorganised (v0.0.1–v0.0.4)

Script header
- Header comments converted to technical English
- VERSION updated to 0.0.4